{"type":"record","name":"StrikeInvasionEventSessionReset","namespace":"com.optionsedge.contracts.strikeinvasion","doc":"One SESSION_RESET record on options.spx.strike-invasion.events (append-only audit stream, keyed 'SPX:<type>' for UP and 'SPX:DOWN:<type>' for DOWN). Until the Avro cutover the topic carried hand-built JSON {seq, ts, type, strike, spot, direction, data:{...}}; this record reproduces it field for field and name for name. The registry subject is this record's full name, so each event type is its own subject on the one topic (RecordNameStrategy). PRICE DOMAIN: every decimal(38,18) field accepts exactly the finite doubles whose shortest round-trip text has at most 18 fractional digits and magnitude below 1e20, and never negative zero; any other value is refused by the codec (never rounded) and the service counts and logs the refusal instead of publishing.","fields":[{"name":"seq","type":"long","doc":"Deterministic per-engine sequence number."},{"name":"ts","type":"double","doc":"Tick-clock time in seconds (event time / 1000.0), printed as the JSON number it always was."},{"name":"type","type":"string","doc":"Always 'SESSION_RESET' on this record type."},{"name":"strike","type":{"type":"bytes","logicalType":"decimal","precision":38,"scale":18},"doc":"REAL strike, 0 for events not tied to a strike."},{"name":"spot","type":{"type":"bytes","logicalType":"decimal","precision":38,"scale":18},"doc":"Spot rounded to cents, REAL space (0 where the event carries none)."},{"name":"direction","type":"string","doc":"UP or DOWN."},{"name":"data","type":{"type":"record","name":"StrikeInvasionSessionResetData","doc":"The engine reset for a new ET trading date.","fields":[{"name":"session","type":"string"}]},"doc":"Type-specific payload, in the order the engine wrote it."}]}